// A message in a chat. Almost always one WhatsApp delivered -- but ALSO the
// echo of a message this relay itself sent, with `key.from_me` true.
//
// Issue #22: WhatsApp echoes a send to every device on the account except the
// one that sent it. The relay holds ONE device session per account and every
// consumer of the socket shares it, so a send made through MessagingService
// comes from our own device and nothing comes back -- not live, not on the next
// history read. Only the consumer that made the call ever learned the message
// existed, while its receipts reached everyone, naming an id nobody had. So the
// relay publishes the echo its own shape prevents. It is the only MESSAGE on
// this bus that WhatsApp did not produce (the other events the core makes up
// are the `raw` `gap` and `subscription_gap` markers of EventService).
//
// It goes to EVERY subscriber, the caller included: excluding the caller would
// mean the bus knowing who called, and the core has no notion of client
// identity. Drop the duplicate on `key.id`, which a consumer must handle
// anyway, since a replayed event has to land on the same row.
//
// WHICH SENDS ECHO: every one that puts a message in a chat. SendText,
// SendMedia, SendReaction, SendContact, SendInteractiveReply, SendPoll,
// SendPollVote, EditMessage, DeleteMessage with `for_everyone`, PostStatusText,
// PostStatusMedia and RevokeStatus. DeleteMessage for-me sends nothing to the chat (it is an
// app-state mutation), so it has nothing to echo, and neither does
// NewsletterService.SendNewsletterPollVote: a channel vote is an add-on on a
// message, not a message in the channel (issue #26). The payload is always the
// message the send encoded, handed back by the library (upstream #1406), never
// a reconstruction -- including the half the library builds itself (issue #38):
//
//   - EditMessage / DeleteMessage echo their protocol message: `is_edit` or
//     `is_delete`, `protocol_target` naming the edited/revoked message, and
//     `key.id` the edit/revoke stanza's own id, same as the edit another device
//     of the account receives.
//   - SendPollVote echoes the encrypted vote (`pollUpdateMessage`), so `text`
//     is empty and the vote is read from `raw_message` with the poll's secret,
//     like any vote that arrives.
//   - PostStatus* echo with `chat` = `status@broadcast`, and so does
//     RevokeStatus, as a delete (`is_delete`) whose `protocol_target` is the
//     status.
