// with its `raw_message` whole — every id, label and the quoted offer — but
// `text` comes back EMPTY, because `project_content` has no case for
// `buttonsResponseMessage` / `listResponseMessage` /
// `templateButtonReplyMessage` / `interactiveResponseMessage`. This is not
// specific to the echo: an inbound reply from the other side projects the same
// way today. A consumer that mirrors a conversation off `text` alone will show
// a blank row where a tap happened, and must read `raw_message` for these.
// Written down rather than papered over, because the display text IS in the
// payload and looking blank is the kind of gap that reads as a delivery bug.
//
// The echo's `raw_message` is that payload AS THE SEND ENCODED IT, which is not
// byte-identical to what the recipient decrypts. The library's send path hoists
